# 8. Prevent Overlay Self-Capture and Feedback Loops

This requirement is mandatory.

The application must not capture its own Thai replacement overlay and then attempt to translate the Thai text again.

Before every MediaProjection frame capture:

- Temporarily hide the replacement overlay.
- Temporarily hide the floating control bubble and expanded panel if they are visible.
- Capture the original underlying screen.
- Restore the application's overlay windows in a guaranteed `finally` path.

Apply this to:

- Manual capture.
- Full Edition Auto-scroll capture.
- Any other automatic capture route.

Inspect the existing `AppContainer.autoCaptureScheduler` and capture service architecture so the guard is applied consistently.

Avoid permanent overlay removal and recreation on every frame if visibility suspension can be implemented safely.

Prevent stale replacement overlays from remaining over a newly scrolled page while waiting for new OCR/translation results.

Do not use Accessibility to solve overlay self-capture.

Do not introduce additional privileges.

